{"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Tours\/documentation\/Tours\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph\/hamiltonianPath()"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A Hamiltonian path, or nil when there is none (or no vertex): the first one a depth-first"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"backtracking search finds, from each vertex in "},{"code":"vertices","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" order, extending through each"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vertex’s "},{"code":"outEdges","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" in order to an unvisited vertex. Self-loops never help; one vertex is the trivial path. Pruning cuts only subtrees with no"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"solution (an unvisited vertex unreachable, or left without a usable predecessor or"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"successor), so it keeps the order. Without a start the search is run again from each"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vertex in turn until one succeeds, so a graph with no Hamiltonian path costs n searches."}],"sections":[],"metadata":{"title":"hamiltonianPath()","role":"symbol","externalID":"s:14GraphProtocols08DirectedA0P5ToursE15hamiltonianPath5Walks0F0Vy6VertexQz5Edges_5IndexQZGSgyF","roleHeading":"Instance Method","extendedModule":"GraphProtocols","modules":[{"relatedModules":["GraphProtocols"],"name":"Tours"}],"remoteSource":{"fileName":"Hamiltonian.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/Tours\/Hamiltonian.swift#L490"},"fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"hamiltonianPath","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Path","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:5Walks4PathV"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocol